## Forward Hooks

**Worktree-isolated parallel build:** must satisfy this document before enablement — because the precondition trio gates it, and because the worktree-is-not-a-credential-boundary insight above is specifically about this capability. Its `AUTOMATION-ISOLATION.md` entry, including the project's declared high-blast-radius surfaces it may not touch, is written before the first parallel batch runs.

**Gated write-back (the scheduled sentinel's phase-2):** same requirement — credential scope and data-isolation posture declared and minimized before enablement.

**Read-only sentinel (the scheduled sentinel's phase-1):** the read-only sentinel may precede the full precondition regime — but even under its minimal gate, the sentinel must declare a **read-only, minimal credential scope** before its first scheduled run. The earliest automation is precisely where an over-scoped credential becomes a habit. The minimal gate for phase-1 is defined in the operate-sentinel phase-1 recipe (`docs/recipes/operate-sentinel/sentinel-phase-1.RECIPE.md`, § The minimal gate).

**Sibling preconditions:** `core/methodology/rollback-kill-switch.md` defines how an enabled capability is stopped and reverted, and `core/methodology/spend-governance.md` defines what it may spend; this document defines what it runs as and what it can reach. A capability is safe to enable only when all three are satisfied — see `core/governance/KILL-SWITCH.md` and `core/governance/AUTOMATION-ISOLATION.md` together.
